Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:03.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Laboratory dynamos use liquid sodium.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.31,0:00:05.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It flows as easily as water.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.83,0:00:10.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}But a field smudges in it about a hundred\Nthousand times faster than its swirls do.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.07,0:00:17.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Their ratio, one in a hundred thousand,\Nis the {\c&H7AAF1B&}magnetic Prandtl number{\c&HF7F4F2&}, Pm.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.93,0:00:21.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Reaching an Rm of a few\Ntens takes violent stirring.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.20,0:00:26.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The flow's {\c&H7AAF1B&}Reynolds number{\c&HF7F4F2&}, the gauge\Nof turbulence, reaches millions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.08,0:00:30.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So every laboratory dynamo is turbulent.
